1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,335
In the movies: Loki is Thor's adopted brother.

2
00:00:06,375 --> 00:00:14,792
In the myths: not Thor's brother. Laufey is his MOTHER.

3
00:00:14,892 --> 00:00:19,835
The real Norse gods: stranger, darker, funnier.

4
00:00:19,875 --> 00:00:23,240
The REAL Norse gods behind Thor & Loki.

5
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:32,734
Our main sources: two Icelandic books, the Eddas.

6
00:00:32,774 --> 00:00:39,493
Poetic Edda: the Codex Regius, c. 1270.

7
00:00:39,533 --> 00:00:47,871
The poems: probably older, perhaps 800-1100 (debated).

8
00:00:47,911 --> 00:00:55,150
Sent to Denmark 1662. Returned to Iceland 1971.

9
00:00:55,190 --> 00:01:03,212
Prose Edda: Snorri Sturluson, c. 1220.

10
00:01:03,252 --> 00:01:12,034
Written by Christians, ≈200 years after conversion.

11
00:01:12,074 --> 00:01:18,115
Our best window. Not a perfect record.

12
00:01:22,215 --> 00:01:25,007
Thor's name means THUNDER.

13
00:01:25,047 --> 00:01:30,365
Son of Odin and the giantess Jörð, "Earth".

14
00:01:30,405 --> 00:01:35,266
Later sources: a RED beard.

15
00:01:35,306 --> 00:01:43,906
His goats: eaten for dinner, revived by the hammer.

16
00:01:43,946 --> 00:01:49,488
A belt of strength. Iron gloves.

17
00:01:49,528 --> 00:01:55,655
Thor went fishing... and hooked the World Serpent.

18
00:01:55,695 --> 00:02:02,048
To recover his hammer: Thor disguised as a BRIDE.

19
00:02:02,088 --> 00:02:06,448
The god of thunder, in a wedding veil.

20
00:02:10,548 --> 00:02:14,368
Mjölnir began with a Loki prank.

21
00:02:14,408 --> 00:02:24,168
Loki bet his head on a dwarf contest.

22
00:02:24,208 --> 00:02:33,879
A biting fly... and the hammer's short handle.

23
00:02:33,919 --> 00:02:43,810
Loki lost the bet. The dwarf sewed his lips shut.

24
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:50,655
Loki's loophole: the head, but not the neck.

25
00:02:50,695 --> 00:03:00,926
Real Viking-Age hammer pendants. One reads: "This is a hammer."

26
00:03:00,966 --> 00:03:05,336
Miniature hammers in Viking-Age graves.

27
00:03:09,436 --> 00:03:18,068
Father: Fárbauti. MOTHER: Laufey.

28
00:03:18,108 --> 00:03:22,937
Not Odin's adopted son: Odin's BLOOD-BROTHER.

29
00:03:22,977 --> 00:03:28,999
Not Thor's brother: his travelling companion.

30
00:03:29,039 --> 00:03:32,188
A shapeshifter: salmon, mare, old woman.

31
00:03:32,228 --> 00:03:39,146
As a mare: mother of Sleipnir, Odin's eight-legged horse.

32
00:03:39,186 --> 00:03:46,151
Father of Fenrir, the World Serpent, and Hel.

33
00:03:46,191 --> 00:03:51,409
No evidence Loki was ever worshipped.

34
00:03:51,449 --> 00:03:56,553
The most entertaining character... and no worshippers.

35
00:04:00,653 --> 00:04:06,385
Odin gave an eye for a drink of wisdom.

36
00:04:06,425 --> 00:04:11,670
Ravens Huginn and Muninn: Thought and Memory.

37
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:17,660
Nine nights on a windswept tree, to win the runes.

38
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:23,751
Wednesday: Woden's (Odin's) day. Thursday: Thor's day.

39
00:04:23,791 --> 00:04:29,226
Tuesday: Tyr, who lost his hand to Fenrir.

40
00:04:29,266 --> 00:04:32,803
Friday: most likely Frigg's day.

41
00:04:32,843 --> 00:04:35,497
Some link Friday to Freyja instead.

42
00:04:39,597 --> 00:04:48,083
Bifröst: a burning rainbow bridge. Heimdall can hear grass grow.

43
00:04:48,123 --> 00:04:55,875
Loki causes Baldr's death, with mistletoe.

44
00:04:55,915 --> 00:05:02,694
Loki bound beneath a venom-dripping snake.

45
00:05:02,734 --> 00:05:11,123
Sigyn's bowl. His writhing = earthquakes.

46
00:05:11,163 --> 00:05:17,379
Ragnarök: Loki breaks free. Bifröst breaks.

47
00:05:17,419 --> 00:05:22,400
Thor kills the serpent, walks nine steps, and falls.

48
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:34,631
"Nine paces fares the son of Fjorgyn..." (Bellows, 1923)

49
00:05:36,531 --> 00:05:43,451
Marvel's Thor: 1962. Loki joined that same year.

50
00:05:43,491 --> 00:05:52,877
The myths are wilder than the movies.

51
00:05:52,917 --> 00:06:00,739
Which real myth surprised you most? Comment & subscribe.
